---
title: What's Next
description: Further resources for configuring feature flags in the Vonage Video iOS App.
---

Congratulations, you have successfully completed the tutorial! Copy the public VERA backend server URL from this Codespace and paste it into the learning path to generate your certificate of completion — you don't need to keep this Codespace open or the server running afterwards.

## What You Accomplished

- Started the shared backend server in this Codespace and made its port public
- Cloned `vonage-video-ios-app` to your own machine, generated the environment constants, and ran the app in Xcode's Simulator
- Understood the structure of `VERA/Config/app-config.json`, including its `videoSettings`, `audioSettings`, `waitingRoomSettings`, and `meetingRoomSettings` sections
- Edited feature flags in `app-config.json` and regenerated `VERAConfiguration/VERAConfiguration/AppConfig.swift` with `generate-app-config.py`
- Rebuilt the app in Xcode and confirmed your changes in the Simulator

## What's Next

Want to also customize the app's colors, typography, and shape? Continue with the companion **Vonage Video iOS App Theme Customization** tutorial — it picks up from the same local setup and walks through `VERA/Theme/semantics.json`.

